--- !u!114 &978717031
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 978717029}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d6e62d09d4b8974408cafe59aa15f6a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  player: {fileID: 395647805}
  dialogue: {fileID: 643504955}
  parameters:
  - line: To jump, simply arch your back and bend your knees
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.1
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - line: You should feel a little tension in the lower part of the body and that
      is perfectly normal
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - line: Ok, you are doing good. Now, start imagining your feet pushing through
      the ground, that should build the tension you are looking for.
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - line: Not bad, not bad. You should start felling some force coming from your
      feet and an equal but opposite force force coming from the ground.
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - line: Again, perfectly normal, don't be scared, this is a thing called third
      Newton's law. Now, we don't need all the mechanical explanation for how this
      works, just be assured that you are doing great
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - line: Ok, now, for the last part. Just simply keep pushing and,when you feel
      like you are ready, push the "Spacebar" on your keyboard, I'll wait
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 10
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 1132592774}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: JumpTutorial, Assembly-CSharp
          m_MethodName: setDialogueToPlay
          m_Mode: 3
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 1
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
  - line: Ok, I guess you can't find the spacebar? Or maybe there is no spacebar
      on your keyboard
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - line: Ok, don't worry, we can work this out, you don't need to leave a negative
      review just because your keyboard is broken
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - line: 'Here, let me just change the input. '
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 1132592774}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: JumpTutorial, Assembly-CSharp
          m_MethodName: RandomizeJump
          m_Mode: 1
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
  - line: It should appear in the lower part of the screen, see if you can find it.
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 1
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - line: Now you have no excuse. Just jump.
    image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 047ca072feba97649a8e9dfb89d2540a, type: 3}
    speed: 0.03
    showsInSameBox: 0
    endsAutomatically: 1
    waitTime: 2
    stop: 0
    onLineReached:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  interruptPlayer: 0
  isActive: 1
